{
  "title": "74: al-Muddassir المدثر",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الْمُدَّثِّرُۙ‏(1)\n\nO’ thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) covered under thy mantle!\nقُمْ فَاَنْذِرْۙ‏(2)\n\nArise (thou) and warn (mankind)!\nوَرَبَّكَ فَكَبِّرْۙ‏(3)\n\nAnd thy Lord, magnify!\nوَثِيَابَكَ فَطَهِّرْۙ‏(4)\n\nAnd thy raiment, purify!\nوَالرُّجْزَ فَاهْجُرْۙ‏(5)\n\nAnd every kind of abomination, Shun it!\nوَلَا تَمْنُنْ تَسْتَكْثِرُۙ‏(6)\n\nAnd bestow not favours (expecting) that thou mayest receive them back increased\nوَ لِرَبِّكَ فَاصْبِرْؕ‏(7)\n\nAnd for (the sake of) thy Lord (endure every hardship) in patience!\nفَاِذَا نُقِرَ فِى النَّاقُوْرِۙ‏(8)\n\nFor when the Trumpet is beaten\nفَذٰلِكَ يَوْمَئِذٍ يَّوْمٌ عَسِيْرٌۙ‏(9)\n\nThat, that shall be the Day of distress (for those who disbelieve)\nعَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ غَيْرُ يَسِيْرٍ‏(10)\n\nUnto the disbelievers (it shall be) anything other than ease!\nذَرْنِىْ وَمَنْ خَلَقْتُ وَحِيْدًا ۙ‏(11)\n\nLeave Me (to deal with) him whom I created (bare and) alone!\nوَّجَعَلْتُ لَهٗ مَالًا مَّمْدُوْدًا ۙ‏(12)\n\nAnd unto whom I granted wealth in abundance!\nوَّبَنِيْنَ شُهُوْدًا ۙ‏(13)\n\nAnd sons abiding in his presence!\nوَّمَهَّدتُّ لَهٗ تَمْهِيْدًا ۙ‏(14)\n\nAnd unto whom I made (life) adjustably smooth!\nثُمَّ يَطْمَعُ اَنْ اَزِيْدَ  ۙ‏(15)\n\nAnd yet desireth he that I should further add!\nكَلَّا ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ لِاٰيٰتِنَا عَنِيْدًا ؕ‏(16)\n\nNever (it shall be)! for unto Our signs he was a foe!\nسَاُرْهِقُهٗ صَعُوْدًا ؕ‏(17)\n\nSoon will I make him afflicted of a severe punishment\nاِنَّهٗ فَكَّرَ وَقَدَّرَۙ‏(18)\n\nVerily, he thought and determined\nفَقُتِلَ كَيْفَ قَدَّرَۙ‏(19)\n\nBut may he be ruined how he determined\nثُمَّ قُتِلَ كَيْفَ قَدَّرَۙ‏(20)\n\nAgain may be he ruined how he determined!\nثُمَّ نَظَرَۙ‏(21)\n\nThen looked he around!\nثُمَّ عَبَسَ وَبَسَرَۙ‏(22)\n\nThen frowned he and scowled!\nثُمَّ اَدْبَرَ وَاسْتَكْبَرَۙ‏(23)\n\nThen turned he his back and swelled in pride!\nفَقَالَ اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا سِحْرٌ يُّؤْثَرُۙ‏(24)\n\nThen said he: “This is naught but sorcery from of old!\nاِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا قَوْلُ الْبَشَرِؕ‏(25)\n\nThis is naught but the word of a human being!\nسَاُصْلِيْهِ سَقَرَ‏(26)\n\nSoon will I cast him into hell!\nوَمَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا سَقَرُؕ‏(27)\n\nAnd what will make him realize what hell is?\nلَا تُبْقِىْ وَ لَا تَذَرُۚ‏(28)\n\nIt leaveth not nor it spareth (aught)\nلَوَّاحَةٌ لِّلْبَشَرِۖۚ‏(29)\n\nIt shrivelleth a human body!\nعَلَيْهَا تِسْعَةَ عَشَرَؕ‏(30)\n\nAbove it (guardians) are nineteen!\nوَمَا جَعَلْنَاۤ اَصْحٰبَ النَّارِ اِلَّا مَلٰٓئِكَةً وَّمَا جَعَلْنَا عِدَّتَهُمْ اِلَّا فِتْنَةً لِّلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا ۙ لِيَسْتَيْقِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ وَيَزْدَادَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِيْمَانًا وَّلَا يَرْتَابَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ وَالْمُؤْمِنُوْنَۙ وَلِيَقُوْلَ الَّذِيْنَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّرَضٌ وَّالْكٰفِرُوْنَ مَاذَاۤ اَرَادَ اللّٰهُ بِهٰذَا مَثَلًا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُضِلُّ اللّٰهُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَهْدِىْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَمَا يَعْلَمُ جُنُوْدَ رَبِّكَ اِلَّا هُوَ ؕ وَمَا هِىَ اِلَّا ذِكْرٰى لِلْبَشَرِ‏(31)\n\nWe have made not the guardians of the fire other than angels, and We have made not the number save as a trial for those who disbelieve, that certain may be those who have been given the book, and may increase those who believe in (their) faith, and may doubt not those who have been given the book and the believers, and that say those in whose hearts is a distress and the disbelievers: “What meaneth God by this similitude?” Thus doth God alloweth to stray whomsoever He willeth, and guideth He whom He willeth, And knoweth not (any one) the hosts of God save He Himself; And this is naught but a reminder unto mankind\nكَلَّا وَالْقَمَرِۙ‏(32)\n\nNay! By the moon!\nوَالَّيْلِ اِذْ اَدْبَرَۙ‏(33)\n\nAnd by the night when it retreateth!\nوَالصُّبْحِ اِذَاۤ اَسْفَرَۙ‏(34)\n\nAnd by the morn when it brighteneth!\nاِنَّهَا لَاِحْدَى الْكُبَرِۙ‏(35)\n\nVerily it (the Hell) is one of the grievous woes!\nنَذِيْرًا لِّلْبَشَرِۙ‏(36)\n\nA warning (it is) unto mankind!\nلِمَنْ شَآءَ مِنْكُمْ اَنْ يَّتَقَدَّمَ اَوْ يَتَاَخَّرَؕ‏(37)\n\nUnto him among you who desireth to go forward (in goodness) or to remain behind\nكُلُّ نَفْسٍ ۢ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ رَهِيْنَةٌ ۙ‏(38)\n\nEvery soul, for what it earned, is held in pledge!\nاِلَّاۤ اَصْحٰبَ الْيَمِيْنِۛ ؕ‏(39)\n\nSave the people of the Right hand\nفِىْ جَنّٰتٍ ۛ يَتَسَآءَلُوْنَۙ‏(40)\n\nIn gardens shall they be, asking each other\nعَنِ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَۙ‏(41)\n\nAbout the guilty ones\nمَا سَلَكَكُمْ فِىْ سَقَرَ‏(42)\n\nWhat hath brought you into the hell!\nقَالُوْا لَمْ نَكُ مِنَ الْمُصَلِّيْنَۙ‏(43)\n\nThey shall say: “We were not of those who offered the regular prayers (to God)\nوَلَمْ نَكُ نُطْعِمُ الْمِسْكِيْنَۙ‏(44)\n\nAnd we used not to feed the poor!\nوَكُنَّا نَخُوْضُ مَعَ الْخَآئِضِيْنَۙ‏(45)\n\nAnd used we to talk vanities with the vain talkers!\nوَ كُنَّا نُكَذِّبُ بِيَوْمِ الدِّيْنِۙ‏(46)\n\nAnd used we to belie the Day of Judgment!\nحَتّٰٓى اَتٰٮنَا الْيَقِيْنُؕ‏(47)\n\nTill came upon us the Certainty (death)\nفَمَا تَنْفَعُهُمْ شَفَاعَةُ الشّٰفِعِيْنَؕ‏(48)\n\nSo, shall avail them not the intercession of the intercessors!\nفَمَا لَهُمْ عَنِ التَّذْكِرَةِ مُعْرِضِيْنَۙ‏(49)\n\nWhat hath happened then (unto them) that they turn aside from the warning\nكَاَنَّهُمْ حُمُرٌ مُّسْتَنْفِرَةٌ ۙ‏(50)\n\nAs if they were asses affrighted\nفَرَّتْ مِنْ قَسْوَرَةٍ ؕ‏(51)\n\nFleeing from a lion\nبَلْ يُرِيْدُ كُلُّ امْرِئٍ مِّنْهُمْ اَنْ يُّؤْتٰى صُحُفًا مُّنَشَّرَةً ۙ‏(52)\n\nNay! But willeth every one of them that he may be given (the heavenly book) in open pages spread out\nكَلَّا ؕ بَلْ لَّا يَخَافُوْنَ الْاٰخِرَةَ ؕ‏(53)\n\nNay! But they fear not the hereafter!\nكَلَّاۤ اِنَّهٗ تَذْكِرَةٌ ۚ‏(54)\n\nNay! Verily it is a Reminder!\nفَمَنْ شَآءَ ذَكَرَهٗ ؕ‏(55)\n\nSo whosoever willeth may mind it\nوَمَا يَذْكُرُوْنَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّشَآءَ اللّٰهُ ؕ هُوَ اَهْلُ التَّقْوٰى وَاَهْلُ الْمَغْفِرَةِ‏(56)\n\nThey will mind it not unless God willeth; Worthy is He to be feared. And worthy is He to seek refuge to",
  "merits": "Surah al-Muddassir (The Clothed One)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 56 verses. Imam Muhammad al-Baqir (a.s.) has said that the person who recites this Surah in his compulsory prayers will attain a rank near the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) in the hereafter and will be protected from any misfortunes in this world.\nIf this Surah is recited daily and then a dua is made after its recitation, then the dua will be answered and the need will be fulfilled. If one makes dua that he wishes to memorize the whole Qur’an then he will not die until he has memorized it."
}
